: "J. M. Martinis, M. H. Devoret, and J. Clarke, Phys. Rev. Lett. 55, 1543 (1985)."}]}, {"reference": {"misc": ["Equation (15b) is correct to lowest order in 〈θx2〉 and 〈θy2〉. It is exact if 〈θx2〉=0 or 〈θy2〉=0"]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "Equation (15b) is correct to lowest order in 〈θx2〉 and 〈θy2〉. It is exact if 〈θx2〉=0 or 〈θy2〉=0.."}]}, {"reference": {"imprint": {"publisher": "Elsevier"}, "publication_info": {"year": 1997}, "misc": ["in Fluctuations Quantiques", "Science,)"], "authors": [{"full_name": "Devoret, M.H."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "M. H. Devoret, in Fluctuations Quantiques (Elsevier, Science, 1997)."}]}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "88", "artid": "228304", "year": 2002, "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.Lett."}, "misc": ["This noise model also makes the implicit assumption of weak coupling to many environmental modes. For the case of strong coupling and 1/f noise, see"], "authors": [{"full_name": "Paladino, E."}, {"full_name": "Faoro, L."}, {"full_name": "Falci, G."}, {"full_name": "Fazio, R."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "This noise model also makes the implicit assumption of weak coupling to many environmental modes. For the case of strong coupling and 1/f noise, see E. Paladino, L. Faoro, G. Falci, and R. Fazio, Phys. Rev. Lett. 88, 228304 (2002)."}], "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2951599"}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "34", "artid": "158", "year": 1986, "page_start": "158", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.B"}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Esteve, D."}, {"full_name": "Devoret, M.H."}, {"full_name": "Martinis, J.M."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "D. Esteve, M. H. Devoret, and J. M. Martinis, Phys. Rev. B 34, 158 (1986)."}]}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "61", "artid": "237", "year": 1992, "page_start": "237", "journal_title": "Appl.Phys.Lett."}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Zimmerli, G."}, {"full_name": "Eiles, T.M."}, {"full_name": "Kautz, R.L."}, {"full_name": "Martinis, J.M."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "G. Zimmerli, T. M. Eiles, R. L. Kautz, and J. M. Martinis, Appl. Phys. Lett. 61, 237 (1992); J. Ahlers, J. Niemeyer, T. Weimann, H. Wolf, V. A. Krupenin, and S. V. Lotkhov, Phys. Rev. B 53, 13 682 (1996)."}]}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "53", "artid": "13", "year": 1996, "page_start": "13", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.B"}, "misc": ["682"], "authors": [{"full_name": "Ahlers, J."}, {"full_name": "Niemeyer, J."}, {"full_name": "Weimann, T."}, {"full_name": "Wolf, H."}, {"full_name": "Krupenin, V.A."}, {"full_name": "Lotkhov, S.V."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "G. Zimmerli, T. M. Eiles, R. L. Kautz, and J. M. Martinis, Appl. Phys. Lett. 61, 237 (1992); J. Ahlers, J. Niemeyer, T. Weimann, H. Wolf, V. A. Krupenin, and S. V. Lotkhov, Phys. Rev. B 53, 13 682 (1996)."}]}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "84", "artid": "5192", "year": 2000, "page_start": "5192", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.Lett."}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Covington, M."}, {"full_name": "Keller, M."}, {"full_name": "Kautz, R."}, {"full_name": "Martinis, J.M."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "M. Covington, M. Keller, R. Kautz, and J. M. Martinis, Phys. Rev. Lett. 84, 5192 (2000)."}]}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "50", "artid": "1757", "year": 1987, "page_start": "1757", "journal_title": "Appl.Phys.Lett."}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Savo, B."}, {"full_name": "Wellstood, F."}, {"full_name": "Clarke, J."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "B. Savo, F. Wellstood, and J. Clarke, Appl. Phys. Lett. 50, 1757 (1987)."}]}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"year": 1988}, "misc": ["Ph.D. thesis, U.C. Berkeley"], "authors": [{"full_name": "Wellstood, F."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "F. Wellstood, Ph.D. thesis, U.C. Berkeley, 1988."}]}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "51", "artid": "207", "year": 1983, "page_start": "207", "journal_title": "J.Low Temp.Phys."}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Koch, R."}, {"full_name": "Clarke, J."}, {"full_name": "Goubau, W."}, {"full_name": "Martinis, J."}, {"full_name": "Pegrum, C."}, {"full_name": "VanHarlingen, D."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "R. Koch, J. Clarke, W. Goubau, J. Martinis, C. Pegrum, and D. VanHarlingen, J. Low Temp. Phys. 51, 207 (1983)."}]}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "50", "artid": "772", "year": 1987, "page_start": "772", "journal_title": "Appl.Phys.Lett."}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Wellstood, F.C."}, {"full_name": "Urbina, C."}, {"full_name": "Clarke, J."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "F. C. Wellstood, C. Urbina, and J. Clarke, Appl. Phys. Lett. 50, 772 (1987)."}], "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2735121"}}, {"reference": {"misc": ["Flux-noise has been measured for devices at low temperature in a manner where vortices are probably trapped in the superconducting film (Ref. ). In high-Tc devices, when vortices were eliminated through careful film design and low-field cooling, flux noise was greatly reduced (Ref. ). This noise reduction has yet to be demonstrated for low-Tc devices"]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "Flux-noise has been measured for devices at low temperature in a manner where vortices are probably trapped in the superconducting film (Ref. ). In high-Tc devices, when vortices were eliminated through careful film design and low-field cooling, flux noise was greatly reduced (Ref. ). This noise reduction has yet to be demonstrated for low-Tc devices."}]}, {"reference": {"misc": ["(unpublished)"], "authors": [{"full_name": "Stan, G."}, {"full_name": "Field, S."}, {"full_name": "Martinis, J.M."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "G. Stan, S. Field, and J. M. Martinis (unpublished)."}]}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "70", "artid": "2037", "year": 1997, "page_start": "2037", "journal_title": "Appl.Phys.Lett."}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Dantsker, E."}, {"full_name": "Tanaka, S."}, {"full_name": "Clarke, J."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "E. Dantsker, S. Tanaka, and J. Clarke, Appl. Phys. Lett. 70, 2037 (1997)."}]}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "64", "artid": "1824", "year": 1990, "page_start": "1824", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.Lett."}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Devoret, M.H."}, {"full_name": "Esteve, D."}, {"full_name": "Grabert, H."}, {"full_name": "Ingold, G.L."}, {"full_name": "Pothier, H."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "value": "M. H. Devoret, D. Esteve, H. Grabert, G. L. Ingold, and H. Pothier, Phys. Rev. Lett. 64, 1824 (1990)."}]}], "number_of_pages": 10, "referenced_authors_bais": ["G.Falci.1", "J.S.Tsai.1", "J.C.FloresUrbina.1", "J.Clarke.1", "F.C.Wellstood.1", "L.Faoro.1", "E.Paladino.1", "J.Aumentado.2", "Y.Makhlin.1", "A.Shnirman.1", "Y.Nakamura.4", "S.W.Nam.1", "C.D.Chen.1", "John.M.Martinis.1", "Rosario.Fazio.1", "G.Schon.1"], "inspire_categories": [{"term": "Quantum Physics"}], "author_count": 5, "first_author": {"full_name": "Martinis, John M.", "last_name": "Martinis", "first_name": "John M.", "recid": 1933164}, "control_number": 2792340, "dois": [{"source": "APS", "value": "10.1103/PhysRevB.67.094510"}], "earliest_date": "2003-03-25", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Martinis:2003dai"], "abstracts": [{"source": "APS", "value": "We calculate for the current-biased Josephson junction the decoherence of the qubit state from noise and dissipation. The effect of dissipation can be entirely accounted for through a semiclassical noise model that appropriately includes the effect of zero-point and thermal fluctuations from dissipation. The magnitude and frequency dependence of this dissipation can be fully evaluated with this model to obtain design constraints for small decoherence. We also calculate decoherence from spin echo and Rabi control sequences and show they are much less sensitive to low-frequency noise than for a Ramsey sequence. We predict small decoherence rates from 1/f noise of charge, critical current, and flux based on noise measurements in prior experiments. Our results indicate this system is a good candidate for a solid-state quantum computer.Received 26 September 2002DOI:https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.67.094510©2003 American Physical Society", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "APS"}}], "refereed": true, "titles": [{"source": "APS", "title": "Decoherence of a superconducting qubit due to bias noise"}], "facet_author_name": ["1963452_José Aumentado", "1933164_John M. Martinis", "996118_Soonkeon Nam", "2427712_K.M. Lang", "2447957_J.C. Flores-Urbina"], "core": true, "imprints": [{"date": "2003-03-25"}], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:2792340", "updated": "2025-07-21T13:27:42.720500"}, "curated": true, "journal_title_variants": ["Phys.Rev.B", "Phys. Rev. B"]}, "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2792340?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2792340?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2792340?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2792340?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2792340?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2792340?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A2792340"}, "updated": "2025-07-21T13:27:42.720500+00:00", "created": "2024-06-01T14:27:21.529524+00:00", "id": "2792340"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevb.67.094510&size=5&page=1", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevb.67.094510&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevb.67